statement:
Given an integer array `nums`, count the pairs `(seq1, seq2)` of subsequences of `nums` such that:

- both `seq1` and `seq2` are non-empty;
- they are disjoint: no index of `nums` is used by both;
- the greatest common divisor of the elements of `seq1` equals the greatest common divisor of the elements of `seq2`.

The pairs are ordered, so `(seq1, seq2)` and `(seq2, seq1)` count separately, and subsequences are told apart by the indices they use, not by their values. Return the count modulo `10^9 + 7`.

validator:
function validate([nums]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(nums) || nums.length < 1 || nums.length > 200) return 'nums needs 1 to 200 values.';
  if (nums.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 1 || v > 200)) return 'Each value is an integer from 1 to 200.';
  return null;
}

